    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d704">

                <pb facs="0651" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 891.48/50</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Barclay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 520</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received May 17.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Phillips</hi>: With reference to the
                    question of the proposed visit to Persia of Doctor MacCallum’s relief
                    expedition, about which discussion has taken place recently, I write to inform
                    you that we have now received a telegram from the Foreign Office to the effect
                    that the British Government agree that the presence of the committee in Persia
                    is calculated to be useful, in connection with the distribution of the sum of
                    money given to Persia by the United States Government for relief purposes.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office express the hope that Doctor MacCallum will consult with Mr.
                    Marling, the British Minister, on his arrival in Persia. Mr. Marling has had
                    long experience in Persia and an intimate knowledge of present Persian politics,
                    and he will of course be glad to assist Doctor MacCallum with the object of
                    securing that the money to be distributed is not misapplied.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Colville Barclay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
